WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.177
The first function returns the sum of two inputs.

00:00:03.177 --> 00:00:09.197
Twelve plus eight gives twenty, and that returned value is stored in result.

00:00:09.197 --> 00:00:13.592
The second function tries to convert age text to an integer.

00:00:13.592 --> 00:00:18.843
If the conversion fails, it returns the message “Invalid age.”

00:00:19.442 --> 00:00:27.644
These examples combine two important habits: returning reusable results and handling expected errors without crashing

00:00:27.644 --> 00:00:29.523
the entire workflow.
